      "message": "The header still documents `{speed_eos}` as an Arista `speed forced` token with `100gfull (100G)`, and never mentions `speed_forced` / `speed_auto` / `speed_fec`. Since PS15, 100000 maps to `100g-2` + `speed auto` + RS-FEC (network.py:72-81) and the arista operations gate on the three new condition keys (lines 120-125 and 137-142). Trigger: an operator adding a vendor or site recipe from this header writes `if: speed` + `speed forced {speed_eos}`, the pattern the previous patchsets shipped. Impact: at 100G the command is silently dropped (unknown `if` name, see switch_cli.py:219-221) and the port keeps its old speed while the move reports success. Fix: document all four speed keys, the per-vendor mapping, and that `{speed_eos}` is no longer a \u0027speed forced\u0027 token at 100G.",
      "revId": "1fe36c70c70355ad255e294ce49035de3a52471a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
