      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T14:59:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The speed -\u003e EOS token/FEC table is now in the vendor-agnostic driver, and it encodes one fabric\u0027s behaviour: on that POC `speed forced 100gfull` is rejected in favour of `speed auto 100g-2` + RS-FEC, while on other EOS platforms `100g-2`/`speed auto` is not a valid speed group. Trigger: any site on such a platform gets `% Invalid input` on every 100G port. Impact: they cannot configure 100G without patching Python, which breaks #750\u0027s acceptance criterion (\u0027adding/overriding a vendor\u0027s commands requires no Python change\u0027) and repeats the shape of the PS3 `verify_untagged: false` finding - a single fabric\u0027s workaround shipped as the global default. Fix: make this recipe data keyed by vendor (e.g. `speeds: {100000: {mode: auto, token: 100g-2, fec: true}}` next to `connection`, with the driver only exposing generic `speed_forced`/`speed_auto`/`speed_fec`), so a site can override the 100G profile without touching code.",
      "revId": "1fe36c70c70355ad255e294ce49035de3a52471a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
