      "side": 1,
      "message": "`validate()` checks the operation shape but not the `if:` keys inside a command list. An unknown condition name is silently falsy: `entry.get(\"if\")` is truthy, `self.params.get(\"if\")` is None, so line 219-221 skips the command and `run()` still returns True (reproduced: `if: speed_forcd` -\u003e recipe validates, `speed forced` never sent, operation reports success). That is the silent skip #750 says must never happen, and PS15 triples the exposure by adding `speed_forced` / `speed_auto` / `speed_fec`, names that exist only in Python. Fix: define the condition names the driver can produce (a module-level tuple, or a per-vendor `params:` block in the recipe) and raise in `validate()` for anything else; add a test asserting a typo\u0027d `if` fails validation.",
      "revId": "1fe36c70c70355ad255e294ce49035de3a52471a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
